Cumulus
-------

Displays a 14-day weather forecast with minimum and maximum temperatures and
the probability of rain.

Cumulus is a KDE Plasma 6 applet (plasmoid) written in C++ and QML.
Plugin ID: io.github.leghissa.cumulus


-- Requirements --

* Qt >= 6.7 (Core, Gui, Quick)
* KDE Frameworks 6 (I18n, Config) and Extra CMake Modules
* Plasma 6 (libplasma, plasmoidviewer for testing)
* CMake >= 3.16


-- Build instructions --

cmake -S . -B ../Cumulus_build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug
cmake --build ../Cumulus_build

The build assembles the complete applet package in ../Cumulus_build/package:
metadata.json, the QML files and the C++ QML module in
contents/lib/io/github/leghissa/cumulus/, which the QML files import by
relative path. The package needs no environment variables or import paths.


-- Installing --

cmake --build ../Cumulus_build --target install-user     # ~/.local, no root
cmake --build ../Cumulus_build --target install-system   # /usr, asks for the password (pkexec)
cmake --build ../Cumulus_build --target uninstall-user
cmake --build ../Cumulus_build --target uninstall-system

The applet is installed as one directory:
<prefix>/share/plasma/plasmoids/io.github.leghissa.cumulus/
All targets restart plasmashell afterwards, so the change is visible
immediately. Then add "Cumulus" to a panel or the desktop via
"Add Widgets…".

The plain "install" and "uninstall" targets (e.g. "Install" in KDevelop)
follow the CMake cache variable CUMULUS_INSTALL_MODE: USER (default) or
SYSTEM. Further settings:

* CUMULUS_USER_PREFIX     prefix of the user install, default ~/.local
* CUMULUS_SYSTEM_PREFIX   prefix of the system install, default /usr
* CUMULUS_RESTART_PLASMASHELL=OFF   never restart plasmashell
* environment variable CUMULUS_NO_RESTART=1   skip the restart once

A user install takes precedence over a system install of the same applet.
Installs with DESTDIR (packaging) never restart plasmashell.


-- Testing & Developing --

From the command line, run the freshly built applet without installing it:

tools/run-plasmoidviewer.sh

The script starts "plasmoidviewer -a ../Cumulus_build/package --formfactor
planar". Set CUMULUS_BUILD_DIR to use a different build directory. Any
arguments are passed on to plasmoidviewer instead of the default, e.g.:

tools/run-plasmoidviewer.sh --formfactor vertical --location leftedge

plasmoidviewer forgets the applet configuration on every start and every
form factor switch. To test with a configured location, install the applet
and use plasmawindowed, which keeps its configuration:

CUMULUS_NO_RESTART=1 cmake --build ../Cumulus_build --target install-user
plasmawindowed io.github.leghissa.cumulus

Unit tests:

ctest --test-dir ../Cumulus_build --output-on-failure

Launch configuration in KDevelop:

1. Run > Configure Launches...
2. Select the project "Cumulus" and add a new "Compiled Binary" launch.
3. Executable: choose "Executable" and enter the absolute path to
   tools/run-plasmoidviewer.sh in this repository.
4. Arguments: leave empty.
5. Working Directory: the repository root.
6. Dependencies: add the project "Cumulus" and set the action to "Build",
   so every launch builds the applet first.
7. Save, then start it with Run > Execute Launch (Shift+F9).


-- Translations --

Messages.sh extracts translatable strings (translation domain
plasma_applet_io.github.leghissa.cumulus) for KDE's i18n tooling.


